<title>GERMANY: Trinkaus 9-mo gp oper profit up 24 pct.</title>
<headline>Trinkaus 9-mo gp oper profit up 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    115.0  vs 92.9</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		     20.7   vs 22.9</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 186.6  vs 177.7</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     146.0  vs 128.6</p>
<p>    Group administration costs		224.7  vs 215.0</p>
<p>    Parent oper profit after provs	  67.1   vs 56.2</p>
<p>    Parent risk provisions		    27.5   vs 25.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Trinkaus &amp; Burkhardt KGaA, a subsidiary of HSBC Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
